#* {{quote-book|en|author=Eknath Easwaran|authorlink=Eknath Easwaran|chapter=12|title=A More Ardent Fire: From Everyday Love to Love of God|location=Tomales, Calif.|publisher=Nilgiri Press|month=May|year=2000|page=142|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dxcNUISHyXEC&pg=PT142|isbn=978-1-888314-03-8|passage=Most of us do not think of excitement as a problem. After all, doesn't everybody like to be on '''cloud number nine'''? I agree: if we could stay on '''cloud number nine''', life might be very pleasant. But, as all of us know, the cloud eventually evaporates. Then we not only come abruptly back to earth; we usually burrow right into its depths and hide&nbsp;– that is, we go into a depression.}}